blurb = "Depicts Saigyō Hōshi (1118-1190), a Japanese poet and monk who lived during the late Heian and early Kamakura period. He lived much of his life as a hermit, but is known for the many long, poetic journeys he took to Northern Honshū that would later inspire the great poet Matsuo Bashō."
